    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155-a8">

                <pb facs="0355" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1902app1/pg331"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Harmon to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington,
                                D. C</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1896-03-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 21,
                    1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of the 17th instant, inclosing a copy of the complaint of
                    Captain Dahlberg, a Russian subject, commander of the Russian bark <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hans</hi>, alleging that he was arrested and detained in
                    prison on a warrant in a civil case issued by the United States court for the
                    southern district of Mississippi, and requesting that I will inform the
                    Department as to the proceedings complained of.</p>
                <p>I will at once communicate with the United States attorney for the southern
                    district of Mississippi, and obtain through him all information he may be able
                    to procure, and will then report more fully, in compliance with your
                    request.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Judson W. Harmon</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Attorney-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
